#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa gamit ang maliit na simulator {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial implements a [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) to simulate a one-dimensional (1D) Many-Body Localization (MBL) circuit. The MBL circuit is a hardware-efficient circuit and is parameterized by two parameters $\\theta$ and $\\vec{\\phi}$. When $\\theta$ is set to $0$ and the initial state is prepared in $|0\\rangle$ for all the qubits, the ideal expectation value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ is $+1$ for every qubit site $i$ irrespective of the values of $\\vec{\\phi}$. More details on this circuit are available in this [article](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-57623-x).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad ng tutorial na ito ang isang [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) upang i-simulate ang isang one-dimensional (1D) Many-Body Localization (MBL) circuit. Ang MBL circuit ay isang hardware-efficient circuit na may dalawang parameter, $\\theta$ at $\\vec{\\phi}$. Kapag ang $\\theta$ ay nakatakda sa $0$ at ang initial state ay inihanda sa $|0\\rangle$ para sa lahat ng qubits, ang ideal expectation value ng $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ ay $+1$ para sa bawat qubit site $i$ anuman ang mga halaga ng $\\vec{\\phi}$. Mas maraming detalye tungkol sa circuit na ito ay makikita sa [artikulong ito](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-57623-x).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that in a noiseless simulator, the expectation value obtained with and without circuit cutting will be same.\n"
msgstr "Pansinin na sa isang noiseless simulator, ang expectation value na nakuha na may at walang circuit cutting ay magiging pareho.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang classical inputs sa quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct the 1D MBL circuit {#construct-the-1d-mbl-circuit}"
msgstr "Buuin ang 1D MBL circuit {#construct-the-1d-mbl-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we present a function for constructing the 1D MBL circuit.\n"
msgstr "Una, nagpapakita tayo ng function para sa pagbuo ng 1D MBL circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/a3debf65-06df-4277-933e-14b6f6170756-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/a3debf65-06df-4277-933e-14b6f6170756-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We calculate the average expectation value $O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_i Z_i$ over all qubits for $\\theta = 0$. Since the ideal expectation value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = 1$ $\\forall$ $i$, the ideal expectation value of $O$ is also $1$. The parameters $\\phi$ are selected randomly.\n"
msgstr "Kinakalkula natin ang average na expectation value na $O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_i Z_i$ sa lahat ng qubits para sa $\\theta = 0$. Dahil ang ideal na expectation value ng $\\langle Z_i \\rangle = 1$ $\\forall$ $i$, ang ideal na expectation value ng $O$ ay $1$ din. Ang mga parameter na $\\phi$ ay pinili nang random.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit needs to be annotated by inserting **CutWire** in the desired locations to partition it. For this tutorial, we opt for equal partition. The MBL circuit is designed so that setting `use_cut=True` in the function inserts the annotation properly after $\\frac{n}{2}$ qubits, $n$ being the number of qubits in the original circuit. We also assigned the randomly generated parameters to the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang circuit ay kailangang markahan sa pamamagitan ng paglalagay ng **CutWire** sa mga ninanais na lokasyon upang hatiin ito. Para sa tutorial na ito, pumipili tayo ng pantay na partisyon. Ang MBL circuit ay dinisenyo upang ang pagtatakda ng `use_cut=True` sa function ay wastong naglalagay ng annotation pagkatapos ng $\\frac{n}{2}$ qubits, kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubits sa orihinal na circuit. Itinalaga rin natin ang mga random na nabuong parameter sa circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/5208e0a8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/5208e0a8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cut the circuit into smaller subcircuits {#cut-the-circuit-into-smaller-subcircuits}"
msgstr "Putulin ang circuit sa mas maliit na subcircuits {#cut-the-circuit-into-smaller-subcircuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we partition the circuit into two smaller subcircuits using [`qiskit-addon-cutting`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/). `qiskit-addon-cutting` appends a virtual `Move` gate to split the wire cut location by appropriately adjusting the number of qubits. Now we create the circuit with this virtual gate. Since there is one wire cut, the number of associated qubits will be increased by 1.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay hinahati natin ang circuit sa dalawang mas maliit na subcircuits gamit ang [`qiskit-addon-cutting`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/). Ang `qiskit-addon-cutting` ay nagdadagdag ng virtual na `Move` gate upang hatiin ang lokasyon ng wire cut sa pamamagitan ng wastong pag-aayos ng bilang ng qubits. Ngayon ay lumilikha tayo ng circuit na may virtual na gate na ito. Dahil may isang wire cut, ang bilang ng mga nauugnay na qubits ay dadagdagan ng 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/1834cb22-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/1834cb22-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct and expand the observable {#construct-and-expand-the-observable}"
msgstr "Buuin at palawakin ang observable {#construct-and-expand-the-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The observable, as defined before, will be the average of $Z$ on each qubit. However, upon inserting the virtual `Move` gate, the effective number of qubits in the circuit increases. The observable must also be expanded accordingly to account for this change in the number of qubits. Note the observable always acts trivially (as in $I$) on the extra qubit added for the virtual `Move` gate.\n"
msgstr "Ang observable, tulad ng tinukoy dati, ay magiging average ng $Z$ sa bawat qubit. Gayunpaman, kapag nailagay na ang virtual na `Move` gate, ang epektibong bilang ng qubits sa circuit ay tumataas. Ang observable ay kailangang palawakin din nang naaayon upang isaalang-alang ang pagbabagong ito sa bilang ng mga qubits. Pansinin na ang observable ay palaging kumikilos nang trivially (bilang $I$) sa karagdagang qubit na idinagdag para sa virtual na `Move` gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the circuit can be partitioned along the `Move` gate and we obtain the subcircuits, as well as the subobservable, which is the portion of the original observable associated with each subcircuit.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay maaari nang hatiin ang circuit sa kahabaan ng `Move` gate at makukuha natin ang mga subcircuits, pati na rin ang subobservable, na siyang bahagi ng orihinal na observable na nauugnay sa bawat subcircuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we visualize the two subcircuits:\n"
msgstr "Dito natin biswalhin ang dalawang subcircuits:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/1b0e779f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/1b0e779f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/3c802f28-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-cutting/extracted-outputs/3c802f28-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expanding the observable using the `Move` operation requires a `PauliList` data structure. To reconstruct the expectation value of the original circuit, we require the observable in the `SparsePauliOp` format.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpapalawak ng observable gamit ang `Move` operation ay nangangailangan ng `PauliList` data structure. Upang ma-reconstruct ang expectation value ng orihinal na circuit, kailangan natin ang observable sa format na `SparsePauliOp`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As discussed before, for each cut the upstream circuit must be measured in a Pauli basis, and the downstream circuit must be prepared in the eigenstate of the basis. The function `generate_cutting_experiments` creates all of these necessary circuits and the coefficients associated with each circuit required for reconstruction. Find more detail in [this paper](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.150504).\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng tinalakay dati, para sa bawat pagputol ang upstream circuit ay kailangang sukatin sa isang Pauli basis, at ang downstream circuit ay kailangang ihanda sa eigenstate ng basis. Ang function na `generate_cutting_experiments` ay lumilikha ng lahat ng kinakailangang circuits at mga coefficients na nauugnay sa bawat circuit na kinakailangan para sa reconstruction. Hanapin ang mas maraming detalye sa [papel na ito](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.150504).\n"

